"""Render the R7 hand-back from checked records; does not grant acceptance."""
import json
from analysis_sources import A,WB,ROOT,digest

def main():
 read=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text());v=read(WB/'checks/r7/final-validation.json');g=read(A/'textbook-gap-search-r7.json');pairs=read(WB/'checks/r7/disputed-pair-review.json');families=read(A/'empty-demand-families-r7.json');author=read(WB/'tools/textbook-relation-decisions-r7.json')
 clean=lambda s:str(s).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
 lines=['# Repair round 7 — NSSCAS Mathematics 8227','','AUTHOR hand-back for Claude’s short cross-vendor check. Step 3 remains blocked on that acceptance. No PLAN, recipes, runtime generators, work orders, imports, commits or push are made by this repair.','','## Scope and baseline','','The frozen R6 snapshot is preserved as `analysis/history/analysis-snapshot-r6.json`, SHA256 `13dcf9f7b0377ff760324e4f0847dd17c7c3be4f21991c547124bb9e5e818464`. Previously accepted scope is retained. Source PDFs, named protected review inputs and accepted item-level demand links are checked unchanged.','','## Finding dispositions','','| Finding / prompt section | Repair | Evidence and check |','|---|---|---|',
 '| R6-01 / A | Direct searches of both books for all 22 named parts; selected-response relations and bounded negative searches | `analysis/textbook-gap-search-r7.json/.md`; R7 gap validator; table below |',
 '| R6-02 / B.1 | Reconsidered all 202 nonordered main decisions and six retained named exceptions; mixed branches allowed with named differences, specific rejection where more than two substantive changes remain | `tools/textbook-relation-decisions-r7.json`; current assembled ledger; rejection negative |',
 '| R6-02 / B.2–3 | Fresh native-page reread of 28 entries (27 unique pairs); values, coefficients and inner function kind alone do not create branches; PAIR-024 same type | `checks/r7/disputed-pair-review.json/.md`; table below; page/hash/date checks |',
 '| R6-02 / B.4–5 | Template rejection annotations using extracted exam text and reused source summaries; recorded R6 closing text restored in the close-out; neutral relation-not-established labels; no stale no-verified-relation phrase | R7 relation input, map and insights; checks cover task pointers and neutral output; templates are not comparison evidence |',
 '| R6-03 | Same-type lower-bound caveat retained; full bank relabel not commissioned | Current ledger/map limitations; no unsupported completeness claim |',
 '| R6-04 / C | All original 61 empty-demand families dispositioned: four gain limited assessed demands; 57 have reasons. Implicit given-point gradient adds D01 from native selected responses without item retags | `analysis/empty-demand-families-r7.json/.md`; 23 new family candidates decided; exact exception guards |',
 '| R6-05 / D.1–2 | Named memberships moved/split; exponential duplicate merged with a retired alias; 428 doubled prefixes removed; two precision contradictions fixed; author-descriptor limits retained | R7 family input and migration audit; all 5,744 response pairs and multiplicities conserved |',
 '| R6-05 / D.3 | Original tan²x restored, finite result √3/3−π/6 independently recomputed; incorrect printed key remains registered. Native confirmations of the two Example 12 source defects; completed forms/positive angles/full sketch keys | `analysis/textbook-corrections-r7.json`; source repair input; canonical author scripts; independent checks and negatives |',
 '| R6-05 / D.4–5 | Two key-page locators and four page observations fixed; consistent division graphic rule, vector-grid diagram medium and explicit own-sketch readback | R7 source overlay/audit; source checker and retained figure negatives |',
 '| R6-05 / D.6 | Cosine quadratic corrected; held principal-inverse original excluded from design anchors and Cambridge comparators named | Named relation correction; rebuilt insights/map; held-anchor negative |',
 '| R6-06 / D.7 | All 3,940 note fields conservatively quarantined; R6 claim corrected to 1,034 spacing edits, not full notes repair | `notes_text_status` and `notes_are_design_evidence:false`; R6 report correction banner, preserved original in history |',
 '| R6-07 / D.8 | Historical status strings clarified; final map hashes final inventory; provenance 037 spacing restored | R7 final checker and build order; regenerated provenance |','','## Counts before and after','','Main family decisions and selected-member exception rows are counted separately in the JSON. The relation-kind totals below include both; a family/part can have more than one selected-response exception. Mixed branches are structural branches, not an extra relation kind.','','| Measure | R6 | R7 |','|---|---:|---:|']
 b=v['counts']['before'];a=v['counts']['after']
 for label,x,y in [('Main decisions',b['main_decisions'],a['main_decisions']),*[(k,b['relations_all_rows'].get(k,0),a['relations_all_rows'].get(k,0))for k in ['same type','structural branch','rejected']],('Mixed branch rows',0,a['mixed_branch_rows']),('Exam parts without any textbook relation',b['parts_without_any_relation'],a['parts_without_any_relation']),('Demands with same-type textbook practice',b['same_type_demands'],a['same_type_demands'])]:lines.append(f'| {label} | {x} | {y} |')
 lines+=['','Families: 500 before; 501 active + 1 retired alias after. All original 61 empty-demand families have individual dispositions; four assigned direct demands and compared, 57 justified supporting/qualified records. Source response pairs remain 5,744; accepted item records remain 3,940.','','The original 22 named syllabus-gap parts resolve as 19 active positive parts, two held intended-type comparisons, and one bounded negative search. Prior/ability-only parts are outside the 22 and remain separately visible in the full no-relation list. Any held original stays internal and cannot be a usable learner/design anchor.','','### Batch-count reconciliation','','The reviewer reported 389 batch-worded records. The exact two literal examples select a different set; a broader documented predicate selects '+str(len(author['batch_rejection_rewrites']))+' main/exception records. All of that superset was rewritten, with original reasons and actual target-source hashes retained. `batch_selection` in the author input records the predicates and counts. This is not a claim of '+str(len(author['batch_rejection_rewrites']))+' new native-page rereads; wrong-part cases and the 28 disputed entries have separate fresh reads.','','## Direct textbook search: 22 parts','','Textbook originals remain internal. A selected response does not certify every response in its family. A no-match result is bounded to the recorded searches, not proof of total absence.','','| Exam part | Decision / source | Reason / search limit |','|---|---|---|']
 for r in g['parts']:
  selected='; '.join(x['item_id']+' ['+', '.join(x['part_labels'])+']'for x in r.get('selected_textbook_items',[]))
  lines.append('| '+clean(r['part_id'])+' | '+clean(r['decision']+('; '+selected if selected else''))+' | '+clean(r['reason']+' '+r.get('search_notes',''))+' |')
 lines+=['','## Fresh reread: 28 disputed entries','','PAIR-020 and PAIR-068 are two reviewer entries for the same family/part; both remain in this table. Each native source and exam page is hashed and dated in the author records.','','| Pair | Decision | Agree with reviewer? | Reason |','|---|---|---|---|']
 for r in pairs['pairs']:lines.append('| '+r['pair']+' | '+clean(r['new_relation']+(' ('+r['difficulty_relative_to_exam']+')'if r.get('difficulty_relative_to_exam')else''))+' | '+('yes'if r['agree_with_reviewer']else'no')+' | '+clean(r['reason'])+' |')
 lines+=['','## Rebuild and check evidence','']
 proof=WB/'checks/r7/fresh-copy-proof.json'
 if proof.exists():
  p=read(proof);lines+=['Fresh relocated-copy proof: `checks/r7/fresh-copy-proof.json`. '+p['status']+'.','']
 else:lines+=['Fresh relocated-copy proof has not yet been written. This report must not be presented as final completion until it passes.','']
 for name in ['final-validation.json','legacy-negative-protections.json','parallel-sources/validation.json','family-negative-validation.json','rebuild-verification-r7.json']:
  path=WB/'checks/r7'/name
  if path.exists():lines.append('- `checks/r7/'+name+'`, SHA256 `'+digest(path)+'`.')
 lines+=['','Four commissioned negatives reject: unmatched part without a search note; nonordered rejection without a specific reason; empty-demand family without its reason; doubled comparison prefix. Earlier fixture suites remain in the runner with the changed mixed-direction policy documented.','','## Limits and next action','','The repaired analysis remains author evidence. The bounded negative search, overlapping item-demand classifications, family descriptor templates, internal textbook rights and quarantined note text remain explicit. All figure content checks remain unchecked where no content-level review occurred; medium comparison does not certify figure or task equivalence. No runtime or production acceptance is claimed.','','Claude should perform the commissioned short check of the R7 gap searches, disputed decisions and named fixes. Only acceptance unlocks step 3: the recipe contract and pilot PLAN.']
 (WB/'checks/repair-r7-report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print('R7 report rendered')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
